Dear Colleagues,

It is our pleasure to introduce the first journal on multimedia retrieval:

The International Journal of Multimedia Information Retrieval (IJMIR)
published by Springer together with Leiden University.

http://www.springer.com/computer/journal/13735
(the site is now open for paper submissions)

There are 3 paper categories:
    - Regular Research Papers (up to 14 pages)
    - Short Research Papers (up to 8 pages)
    - Trends and Surveys (up to 20 pages)

with an expected average decision time of 3 months.

The International Journal of Multimedia Information Retrieval 
is a scholarly archival journal publishing original, peer-reviewed 
research contributions. Its editorial board strives to present 
the most important research results in areas within the field 
of multimedia information retrieval.  Core areas include 
exploration, search, and mining in general collections of 
multimedia consisting of information from the WWW to scientific 
imaging to personal archives. 

The success of the journal will depend on the quality of the
submissions and so we hope that you will submit some of your
high quality papers.  

Sincerely,

The IJMIR Editorial Board

